From: BanaNAS <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: sun7i-a20-bananapro: pin CPU clock to 912 MHz

The upstream sun7i-a20-bananapro.dts leaves cpu@0 and cpu@1 without a
clock-frequency property, which makes the kernel emit
  /cpus/cpu@0 missing clock-frequency property
at boot. Pin both cores to the 912 MHz operating point that U-Boot
SPL already configures the PLLs for, matching what the LeMaker
reference setup uses.

Signed-off-by: BanaNAS <noreply@example.invalid>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-bananapro.dts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-bananapro.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-bananapro.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-bananapro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun7i-a20-bananapro.dts
@@ -217,3 +217,11 @@
 	usb2_vbus-supply = <&reg_usb2_vbus>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&cpu0 {
+	clock-frequency = <912000000>;
+};
+
+&cpu1 {
+	clock-frequency = <912000000>;
+};
